Strings aur User Input (input())
Aaj hum seekhenge:

String kya hoti hai?
User se input kaise lete hain?

1. String kya hoti hai?
Jo bhi text double quotes (" ") ya single quotes (' ') me likha jata hai, use String kehte hain.

Example:
name = "Vijay"

print(name)

output:
Vijay

2. User Input (input())
Ab tak tum khud value likhte the.
Ab user keyboard se value enter karega.

Example:
name = input("Enter Your Name: ")

print("Hello", name)

Agar user likhe:
Vijay

output:
Hello Vijay

Trading Example
stock = input("Enter Stock Name: ")

print("Selected Stock:", stock)

Agar user likhe:
TCS

output:
Selected Stock: TCS

4. Multiple Inputs
name = input("Enter Name: ")
stock = input("Enter Stock: ")

print(name)
print(stock)

Agar user likhe:
vijay
nvda

output:
vijay
nvda

Ek chhoti si baat
Abhi input() se jo value aati hai, wo text (string) hoti hai. Agar tum usse calculation me use karoge, to error aa sakta hai.

